==================================================================
DAY 17 - PART B: LAB
Resolve names inside the cluster
Time: 75-90 minutes
==================================================================

cd ~/k8s-journey/manifests/week3


STEP 1: Find CoreDNS
--------------------
k get deploy,svc -n kube-system -l k8s-app=kube-dns
k get pods -n kube-system -l k8s-app=kube-dns -o wide
k get cm coredns -n kube-system -o yaml

Read the Corefile: "kubernetes cluster.local ...", "forward .
/etc/resolv.conf", "cache 30".


STEP 2: Set up two namespaces
-----------------------------
k create ns shop
k apply -f backend.yaml -f backend-svc.yaml -n shop
k create ns frontend
k run tool -n frontend --image=nicolaka/netshoot -- sleep infinity
k get pods -n shop
k get pods -n frontend


STEP 3: Look at resolv.conf
---------------------------
k exec -n frontend tool -- cat /etc/resolv.conf

Note nameserver = kube-dns ClusterIP, and the search list starts with
"frontend.svc.cluster.local".


STEP 4: Short, medium, and full names
-------------------------------------
k exec -n frontend tool -- nslookup backend
   -> fails: there is no "backend" in namespace frontend
k exec -n frontend tool -- nslookup backend.shop
   -> works
k exec -n frontend tool -- nslookup backend.shop.svc.cluster.local
   -> works
k exec -n frontend tool -- curl -s backend.shop


STEP 5: Watch the search-domain lookups
---------------------------------------
k exec -n frontend tool -- dig +search +showsearch backend.shop

You see each try: backend.shop.frontend.svc.cluster.local (NXDOMAIN),
backend.shop.svc.cluster.local (answer).

k exec -n frontend tool -- dig +search +showsearch kubernetes.io
Count the failed tries before the real lookup (ndots:5 effect).

k exec -n frontend tool -- dig kubernetes.io.     (trailing dot = 1 lookup)


STEP 6: SRV records and headless
--------------------------------
k exec -n frontend tool -- dig +short SRV _http._tcp.backend.shop.svc.cluster.local
k apply -f backend-headless.yaml -n shop
k exec -n frontend tool -- dig +short backend-headless.shop.svc.cluster.local


STEP 7: Pod DNS records
-----------------------
A pod with IP 10.244.1.5 in namespace shop also has:
  10-244-1-5.shop.pod.cluster.local
POD_IP=$(k get pod -n shop -l app=backend -o jsonpath='{.items[0].status.podIP}')
k exec -n frontend tool -- nslookup $(echo $POD_IP | tr . -).shop.pod.cluster.local


STEP 8: CoreDNS logs (enable query logging)
-------------------------------------------
k edit cm coredns -n kube-system
  Add a line "log" inside the ".:53 {" block (e.g. under "errors").
k rollout restart deploy coredns -n kube-system
k exec -n frontend tool -- nslookup backend.shop
k logs -n kube-system -l k8s-app=kube-dns --tail=10

Remove the "log" line afterwards and restart again (logging every
query is noisy).


STEP 9: Break DNS and fix it
----------------------------
k scale deploy coredns -n kube-system --replicas=0
k exec -n frontend tool -- nslookup -timeout=2 backend.shop      # times out
k exec -n frontend tool -- curl -s -m 3 backend.shop              # fails
k exec -n frontend tool -- curl -s -m 3 $(k get svc backend -n shop -o jsonpath='{.spec.clusterIP}')
   -> works by IP: the Service is fine, only DNS is broken

Fix:
  k scale deploy coredns -n kube-system --replicas=2


STEP 10: Custom dnsConfig
-------------------------
vi pod-dnsconfig.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: lowndots
  namespace: frontend
spec:
  dnsConfig:
    options:
    - name: ndots
      value: "1"
  containers:
  - name: tool
    image: nicolaka/netshoot
    command: ["sleep", "infinity"]

k apply -f pod-dnsconfig.yaml
k exec -n frontend lowndots -- cat /etc/resolv.conf
k exec -n frontend lowndots -- dig +search +showsearch kubernetes.io


STEP 11: Clean up and commit
----------------------------
k delete ns shop frontend
cd ~/k8s-journey && git add . && git commit -m "day17: dns"
